# categories.psv -- what each program is FOR.  name | category | subcategory
#
# Hand-maintained on purpose.  DOC/INDEX says what a program IS; this says
# what someone would be looking for when they find it, which no rule gets
# entirely right: `stone` describes itself as a SNOBOL demo and is a game,
# `rain` sits in CMDS/GAMES and is not one, and `game` sounds like checkers
# but carries the chess piece letters PNBRQK.
#
# tools/gen_catalog.py reads this and reports any program missing from it, so
# a new arrival cannot be silently uncategorised.  Fixing a wrong call is a
# one-line edit here rather than a change to a regex that moves ten others.
#
# Keep a category under about 20 entries or give it subcategories; past that
# a reader is back to scanning an alphabetical list.


